# UIUX Quality and Accessibility Rule

## UX quality
- User flows must provide clear state transitions (loading, success, empty, error).
- Interactions must have predictable feedback and error recovery paths.
- Avoid disruptive behavior and inconsistent navigation patterns.

## Accessibility baseline
- Ensure keyboard and screen-reader friendly interaction where applicable.
- Maintain sufficient contrast and readable typography.
- Avoid relying on color-only communication for critical states.

## Product polish
- Keep visual/system consistency across components and screens.
- Prevent UI regressions with targeted checks for key journeys.
- No UI feature marked DONE without UX acceptance evidence.
